# One source, two flavours, because the two shells deliberately do not share a
# dependency set: the GNOME one links no KF6 at all (GNOME_PLAN.md D3 - GNOME
# ships none), the Plasma one uses KF6 for notifications and global shortcuts.
# Both install the same `traduku` binary name and the same .desktop, so they
# conflict: a machine runs the flavour of its desktop.

Package: traduku
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libqt6multimedia6,
 qt6-wayland, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good
Recommends: wl-clipboard
Provides: traduku-gnome (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: traduku-gnome
Description: Clipboard translator powered by any OpenAI-compatible LLM (Plasma)
 Press Ctrl+C twice to translate the clipboard into the configured target
 language. Streams responses, translates interactively. This is the KDE Plasma
 flavour: notifications and global shortcuts go through KF6, the tray is
 Qt's StatusNotifierItem client.
 .
 Any other desktop works too (X11 and Wayland via XWayland), but on GNOME
 prefer traduku-gnome, which pulls in no KF6 and ships the udev rule the
 /dev/input gesture needs.

Package: traduku-gnome
Architecture: any
# wl-clipboard is a hard dependency here, not a recommendation: this shell
# reads the Wayland clipboard through wl-paste, and Qt's own QClipboard cannot
# be used from a background process on Wayland (measured). Without the tool the
# app still runs and says so out loud, but it cannot do its job.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libqt6multimedia6,
 qt6-wayland, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, wl-clipboard
# Not a Recommends: the app runs and translates without any tray host
# (measured on a guest with no extension - gesture, clipboard and FDO
# notifications all work). The extension only decides whether the icon is
# *drawn*, and only on a shell that has no StatusNotifier host of its own;
# Ubuntu ships one out of the box. A user who never touches the tray should
# not be offered a shell extension.
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator | gnome-shell-ubuntu-extensions
Provides: traduku (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: traduku
Description: Clipboard translator powered by any OpenAI-compatible LLM (GNOME)
 Press Ctrl+C twice to translate the clipboard into the configured target
 language. Streams responses, translates interactively. This is the GNOME
 flavour: no KF6 anywhere, notifications over the freedesktop portal/D-Bus,
 the gesture reads /dev/input (the package ships the uaccess rule that grants
 the ACL, so no user is added to the input group), and the clipboard is
 wl-clipboard.
